<title>USA: NordLB 9-month oper profit falls 18 percent.</title>
<headline>NordLB 9-month oper profit falls 18 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>First nine months 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Oper profit after provisions    315.5  vs 384.4</p>
<p>    Oper profit before provisions   515.5  vs 613.4</p>
<p>    Bad debt provisions		 200    vs 229</p>
<p>    Income from own-account trading 29.5   vs 75.9</p>
<p>    Net interest income		 1,250.0vs 1,197.9</p>
<p>    Net commission income	     187.0  vs 162.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Norddeutsche Landesbank Girozentrale (NordLB). The bank is based in Hanover but results were released from Washington, where its management board is for the International Monetary Fund meeting.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
